{title: 185 - Jesus Is All the World to Me}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #185 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 185}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Jesus is [C]all the [D]world to [G]me, My life, my [D]joy, my [G]all;
[G]He [D]is my strength from [G]day to day, With[A7]out Him I would [D]fa[D7]ll.
When I am sad to Him I go; No other one can cheer me so;
[Em]When I am [Eb7]sad [G]He makes me glad, He's [D7]my [G]Friend.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Jesus [C]is [D]all [G]the [D]world [G]to me,
[G][D]my [G]friend [A7]in [D]trials [D7]sore;
I go to him for blessings, and
[Em]he [Eb7]gives [G]them [D7]o'er [G]and o'er.
[G]He [C]sends [D]the [G]sunshine [D]and [G]the rain,
[G]he [D]sends [G]the [A7]harvest's [D]golden [D7]grain;
sunshine and rain, harvest of grain,
[Em][Eb7]he's [G][D7]my [G]friend.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Jesus [C]is [D]all [G]the [D]world [G]to me,
[G]and [D]true [G]to [A7]him [D]I'll [D7]be;
O how could I this friend deny,
[Em]when [Eb7]he's [G]so [D7]true [G]to me?
[G]Following [C]him [D]I [G]know [D]I'm [G]right,
[G]he [D]watches [G]o'er [A7]me [D]day [D7]and night;
following him by day and night,
[Em][Eb7]he's [G][D7]my [G]friend.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Jesus [C]is [D]all [G]the [D]world [G]to me,
[G][D]I [G]want [A7]no [D]better [D7]friend;
I trust him now, I'll trust him when
[Em]life's [Eb7]fleeting [G]days [D7]shall [G]end.
[G]Beautiful [C]life [D]with [G]such [D]a [G]friend,
[G]beautiful [D]life [G]that [A7]has [D]no [D7]end;
eternal life, eternal joy,
[Em][Eb7]he's [G][D7]my [G]friend.
{end_of_verse}
